 "notes": "Ras il-Ħobż headland at the mouth of Mġarr ix-Xini with the Middle Finger pinnacle about 50 m off its tip (top 8–10 m, base 40+ m, a 35 m channel on the shore side, the seaward side falling to 90 m), and one entry on each side of the headland. Layout and depths from maltadives.com, divers-guide.com, divebluewaters.com and nds-malta.com; the shoreline is OpenStreetMap. The pinnacle, entries and route are placed from the text descriptions and are approximate; the engine block and the 63 m anchor the guides mention are not placed.",
